  "summary": "This study compares a porous Ti3CNTx MXene/carbon-dot composite film (p-MC), a pure Ti3CNTx MXene-film control, and an authors-fabricated activated-carbon (AC) positive electrode for asymmetric devices. Ti3CNTx was obtained by LiF/HCl etching of Ti3AlCN; p-MC was made by carbon-dot mixing, vacuum filtration, and 350 \u00b0C annealing, where carbon-dot pyrolysis generated NH3 for in situ pore etching. The headline p-MC electrode delivered 688.9 F g\u22121 at 2 A g\u22121 in 1 M H2SO4, versus 283.7 F g\u22121 for pure MXene at the same current density. The paper describes optimization of fresh and annealed MC films across carbon-dot contents, but the supplied text does not provide individually resolved sample labels or capacitance values for those optimization variants; numerical mass loading, thickness, BET area, porosity, pore diameter, and interlayer spacing are also absent."
